syntax:
Multiplication is performed before addition.
result = 5 + 3 * 2;
result = 11

Parentheses cause the addition to be performed first.
result = (5 + 3) * 2;
result = 16

Multiplication and division have the same precedence, so they are evaluated from left to right.
result = 20 / 5 * 2;
result = 8

Modulus has the same precedence as multiplication and division.
result = 10 + 7 % 4;
result = 13

