Use a manipulator to display a floating-point value in fixed-point notation.
double price = 12.5;
cout << fixed << price;

Create columns by setting the width of each value.
cout << setw(15) << "Name" << setw(10) << "Grade" << endl;
cout << setw(15) << "Alex" << setw(10) << 95 << endl;

Display a floating-point value using fixed-point notation.
