cout << fixed << value;

Display exactly two digits after the decimal point.
double price = 12.3456;
cout << fixed << setprecision(2) << price;
// Outputs 12.35

Set the number of significant digits.
double value = 12.3456;
cout << setprecision(4) << value;
// Outputs 12.35

Use fixed to set the number of digits after the decimal point.
