examples:
Sort an entire array using begin() and end():

int numbers[5] = {42, 15, 73, 8, 31};

std::sort(begin(numbers), end(numbers));

The resulting array is:
8, 15, 31, 42, 73

Sort an entire array using the + operator:

int numbers[5] = {42, 15, 73, 8, 31};

std::sort(numbers, numbers + 5);

The resulting array is:
8, 15, 31, 42, 73

Sort only part of an array:

int numbers[5] = {42, 15, 73, 8, 31};

