double value2 = Statistics::calculate(10.0);

Although both functions are named calculate(), the qualified names identify which namespace function should be called.

Members of the std namespace can also be accessed with the scope resolution operator:

std::string name = "Alex";
std::cout << name << std::endl;

Access standard library members using their qualified names:

#include <iostream>
#include <string>

int main()
{
    std::string name;

    std::cout << "Enter your name: ";
    std::cin >> name;

    std::cout << "Hello " << name << std::endl;

    return 0;
}

The header file and namespace serve different purposes:

#include <iostream>

std::cout << "Hello" << std::endl;

#include <iostream> makes the standard input/output declarations available, while std:: identifies cout and endl as members of the standard namespace.

